# Last Call Result

The IESG received feedback from the community in response to the IETF Last Call on the proposed RFC 3683 PR-action for Ken Kubota [1]. After evaluating this feedback, the IESG has concluded there is rough consensus to proceed with the PR-action.

Per the terms described in Section 2 of RFC 3683, the administrators of the ietf, tls, sshm, and mod-discuss lists are directed to suspend Ken Kubota’s posting privileges.  Additionally, this same section advises “maintainers of any IETF mailing list may, at their discretion, also remove posting rights to that IETF mailing list.”

# Highlights from the Community Feedback

The IESG thanks the community for providing this feedback and highlights the following feedback.

## Additional Justification for Action

In addition to the messages outlined in [1], the following additional message was requested during the IETF Last Call to be added to the record motivating this PR action by the community:

* https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/ietf/OrvxKgjrEOMb95KAWoJYSilDxiY/

## Recommendations for PR actions

The community made the following recommendations regarding PR actions:

* Ensuring that the subject of the PR action is directly notified in addition to using the last-call@ietf.org mailing list.

* Harmonizing active PR actions with the new RFC 9945-defined procedures.

## Implementing RFC9945

The community expressed an urgency to fully implement the procedures of RFC 9945.

# Conclusion

The IESG reiterates that the purpose of this action is to minimize disruptive behavior by a single participant.  The IESG also reaffirms that a diverse set of opinions in the standards process is both important for the IETF and actively encouraged.

Per RFC 9945, the IETF Moderator Team [2] is authoring the first draft of the new moderation procedures.  For discussion about IETF moderation procedures use mod-discuss@ietf.org [3].

Roman Danyliw
(as IETF Chair, for the IESG)

